+the shape is real; the hazard is not. a read-modify-write corrupts when **the write is
+derived from the read** (`count = read() + 1`). here every PUT field comes from `desired` —
+**not one comes from `before`**. so an interleave cannot tear state:
+
+- same declaration twice → converges identically (idempotent)
+- different declarations → one whole declared posture wins, never a blend
+- **read-after-write fails loud** on any divergence, which is the opposite of a silent lost
+  update
